This implementation of double-checked locking is inefficient. When multiple goroutines experience a cache miss, they will all queue for the write lock and each will redundantly re-compute the assets. To prevent this, you must re-check if the cache has been populated after acquiring the write lock.

Example:
```go
	entryPointAssetsCacheMu.Lock()
	defer entryPointAssetsCacheMu.Unlock()

	// Re-check if another goroutine populated the cache while we were waiting for the lock.
	if cfg.Env != setting.Dev && entryPointAssetsCache != nil {
		return entryPointAssetsCache, nil
	}
```
